# Gradle tasks in this repository

This repo **is** the `gradle-tapi-mcp-server` MCP provider. Verification strategy depends on what you change.

## Server Kotlin / build script changes

Use **shell `./gradlew`** — not the `gradle` MCP server — while compiling or testing code you are editing:

- Cloud bootstrap runs the **release** JAR from `.cursor/install.sh`; it cannot drive a build of the server you are rewriting in the same session.
- After `./gradlew jar`, restart MCP and point at the local JAR only when you need to **exercise new server behavior** (not for routine compile/test of server changes).

| Goal | Command |
|------|---------|
| Compile + unit tests | `./gradlew build` |
| Tests only | `./gradlew test` |
| Assemble JAR | `./gradlew jar` |
| Single test class | `./gradlew test --tests "com.example.gradle.mcp.build.BuildExecutionManagerRunTest"` |

For long shell builds, run `./gradlew` in a **background shell session** when the client supports it; otherwise one `./gradlew` invocation per verify round. This is separate from MCP `gradle_run_tasks` `background: true` below.

## Docs / `.cursor/` / `AGENTS.md` only (no server code)

Prefer the `gradle` MCP server (release v0.6.0 via `.cursor/mcp.json`) over shell when verifying that the project still builds:

1. `gradle_connection_status` — confirm `connectedAny: true` (or per-connection `connected: true` when a single project is listed)
2. If not connected, `gradle_connect` with `projectDirectory` (defaults to `GRADLE_PROJECT_DIR`) and re-check status
3. `gradle_get_build_environment` or `gradle_get_project_overview` for light context
4. `gradle_run_tasks` with `["build"]`, `background: true` + poll `gradle_get_build_status`

Read `.cursor/skills/gradle-tapi-mcp/SKILL.md` for token-efficient MCP defaults (`includeOutput=false`, batch tests, short polls).

## MCP tool discovery (token-efficient)

When using Cursor **GetMcpTools** (some clients expose this as `mcp_get_tools`):

1. Call with **no arguments** first (catalog only)
2. Fetch full schema with `server` + `toolName` for tools you will call
3. Avoid `server` without `toolName` unless you need every schema

## Shell fallback when MCP is appropriate but unavailable

- MCP tools time out or the server is unresponsive (poll `gradle_list_builds` / `gradle_get_build_status` first)
- `BUILD_ALREADY_RUNNING` and you cannot cancel the in-flight MCP build
- PR / CI parity requires `./gradlew build` after MCP verification passes

Do **not** run MCP `gradle_run_tests` and shell `./gradlew test` on the same checkout concurrently.
